# What of this dist is COMMITTED, and what is only a build by-product.
#
# Ruled 2026-09-01 (lead, A-T4 Finding 3, option c). The committed tree is what
# a CONSUMER needs: include/, the two stripped shared objects, and share/
# (licences + provenance). Everything excluded below is a build INPUT or a
# developer tool, reproducible from the pinned sources by re-running the
# producer workflow.
#
# bin/            -- aomenc (52.8 MB), aomdec (48.9 MB), kvazaar, dec265.
#                    Command-line tools; nothing inside an APK ever runs them.
#                    Same exclusion the other dists make (903ce30 precedent).
# lib/*.a         -- libaom.a (99.55 MB) and libkvazaar.a. These are the STATIC
#                    INPUTS already merged into libheif.so; keeping them would
#                    commit the same code twice. libaom.a measured 99,554,482
#                    bytes on CI run 33460559016 -- under GitHub's 100 MB
#                    per-file hard limit by roughly 450 KB, which is luck, not
#                    headroom, and the wall that rejected the libjxl android
#                    dist push outright.
# lib/pkgconfig/, lib/cmake/ -- build-time discovery files for a prefix layout
#                    that does not exist on the consumer's machine.
#
# .stage/ is the carrier's own scratch directory (downloaded source tarballs).
# deps/heif.py deletes it on a successful assemble; this entry covers the run
# that fails midway, so source archives can never be offered up for commit.
bin/
# share/man/ -- the kvazaar CLI's man page; the CLI itself is excluded above,
# so its manual is documentation for a program this tree does not ship (same
# exclusion the sibling android dists make).
share/man/
lib/*.a
lib/pkgconfig/
lib/cmake/
.stage/
